  <h2>Earlier S60 references are not automatically transferable</h2>
  <p>The <a href="https://www.volvocars.com/mt/support/car/s60/2018/article/a5f51e2cf78bd5abc0a801e800dc8b0b/">Volvo 2018 S60 engine-compartment overview</a> is useful as an example of Volvo's labeled engine-bay illustration style and how service points are presented. It is for the earlier S60 generation, not the 2021 SPA-platform car. Its component positions and callout labels are not used as 2021 fitment data. This reference instead uses Volvo's <a href="https://www.volvocars.com/uk/support/car/s60/2021/article/f3e117dc70239324c0a801513d2de23c/">2021 S60 engine-compartment overview</a> where available.
  </p>

  <h2>Visual-source policy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vehicle photographs:</strong> must show a Volvo S60 from the stated generation/model year. Captions identify year, trim and market when known; meaningful differences such as right-hand drive are disclosed.</li>
    <li><strong>Factory illustrations:</strong> must link to the Volvo source and retain any model-year, market and equipment limitations. A support illustration is not automatically a workshop procedure.</li>
    <li><strong>Conceptual diagrams:</strong> are original explanatory drawings and are labeled as such. They must not be mistaken for exact component locations, dimensions, wiring or service instructions.</li>
    <li><strong>Generic stock imagery:</strong> is not used as a substitute for an S60 component photograph. If a relevant, properly sourced image is unavailable, use no image rather than an unrelated one.</li>
    <li><strong>Parts drawings:</strong> must be tied to a VIN/trim-filtered parts catalogue and labeled with the catalogue's fitment limitations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Photographic references added during the visual audit</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cabin photograph:</strong> Chanokchon, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2020_Volvo_S60_T8_Twin_Engine_AWD_R-Design_(Cockpit).jpg">2020 Volvo S60 T8 Twin Engine AWD R-Design cockpit</a>, CC BY-SA 4.0. The image is a Thailand-market right-hand-drive car; it is labeled as an architecture/material reference, not a North American control-layout guide.</li>
    <li><strong>Underbody photographs:</strong> <a href="https://nrd-static.nhtsa.dot.gov/reports/vehdb/v10000/v11000/v11047R001.pdf">NHTSA/Calspan NCAP-CAL-20-010, 2020 Volvo S60</a>, Figures A-24 and A-26. The report photographs show a test-prepared car with instrumentation; they are linked as reference material rather than republished as repair imagery.</li>
    <li><strong>Brake hardware:</strong> the 2020 U.S. Volvo S60 brochure includes a genuine Polestar Engineered Brembo brake close-up (page 35), but that is a special six-piston performance setup, not the T5 Inscription brakes. The available 2021 T5 Inscription parts catalogues provide VIN/option-dependent diagrams and part listings; no properly licensed close-up photograph of the installed 2021 T5 brake assembly was verified. The site links the Polestar image with a strict variant caveat and keeps its conceptual T5-neutral drawing rather than substituting unrelated hardware.</li>
    <li><strong>Paint damage:</strong> no suitably licensed close-up of actual third-generation S60 paint damage was verified. The page retains its clearly labeled paint-layer diagram rather than using generic damage stock photography.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How corrections are handled</h2>
  <p>When a model-year or market conflict is found, the reference should identify the conflict and defer to the vehicle's VIN-specific information. Do not silently blend data from adjacent model years, hybrid variants, different engines, or different transmissions.</p>
  <p>Before performing a repair, independently verify the latest applicable Volvo procedure, parts, torque values, and safety instructions. This website is an index and owner notebook, not authorization to perform a repair.</p>
